A||N||12||jlhuber||borla exhaust system (long)||||1
Z||000000||jlhuber||10-27-1999||01:01 AM||||for those who are interested in a great exhaust system... i have been looking for an exhaust system for my '86.5 gt for a while now with no luck.  i've heard bad things about the ocelot system so i decided against that system, and i don't want to put a flowmaster on it.  flow's were first built with mainly v8's in mind.  for those of you who like the sound and performance of the flow's...more power to you.  i am not cutting you down, i am just saying i want something that was built with only the fiero in mind.  through years of 4wheelin' i have found that borla systems and components last longer then any other manufacturer i have seen.  if they can hold up to off-road abuse,(aka mud, sand, high heat, sticks, gravel, water) i figured they should do quite well on the street.  i decided that scince most sound good, last practically forever, and they look good, i'll try it on my fiero.  so i gave borla a call.  i found out that borla used to make a system for the fiero but they were only sold through a company called "fiero parts & appraisals," located in maine.  so i called them, thus finding out that the production on these systems has stopped due to "lack of sales."  but the people that once sold these systems are trying to stirr up some intrest again.  if they get enough people, they will do another limited run production of the borla exhaust for the fiero.  the first run was kinda pricey due to the exhaust tips, therefore this time they will be produced without the tips creating a cheaper system that you can add whatever tips you like for your own "personal" tastes. for more information call fiero parts @ 1-800-255-3437, or borla @ 1-800-927-5129 x245 <BR>this website --&gt; <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroparts.com</A>  is the page for fiero parts& appraisals, as pointed out by a fellow member.  if you scroll down the left hand column to the "aftermarket parts" icon and click on it, you can see the system that borla USED to make.  that system is no longer produced.  you can tell because it comes with the tips installed.  the new system, if produced will have no tips from the factory, ...well that is what the rep. from fiero parts says.     <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by jlhuber (edited 10-27-1999).]||||reg||1
