Z||000006||88 Fiero||10-27-1999||01:40 PM||||Bruce no one seems to know the part no. for this flowmaster. They advice me to go to a reputable muffler shop and put the car on the rack or lift and have them fit it with the Camaro RS V6 Flowmaster muffler... It could be the the '87-'89 Camaro RS or the early '90's model. I personally would not spend so much money on a custom exhaust. The Borla exhaust I believe was price around $500.00+ at the Fiero Heaven website. The ones on my car I paid $80.. and it's a complete system for the Fiero starting from the Catalytic converter all the way to the connection of the Exhaust Tips. And I don't experience any problem when I accelerate. Plus, you need some back pressure to get performance. Also the Flowmaster performs as good as Borla.. I would invest more money on my engine than the exhaust...||||reg||1
Z||000007||mwbackus||10-27-1999||02:26 PM||||I believe that the flowmaster part number you are referring to is:<BR>42583<P>It is an 80 Series, single offset 2½" inlet/ 2½" dual outlet, designed for the 82-85 Camaro/Firebird.<BR>The problem is they are a bit too long. :-(<P>Mike||||reg||1
